#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot

id: tp-09-back-to-the-wall
number: 109
name: Back to the Wall
description: The narrow corridor is the only place a Stalker cannot shove you, and it dead-ends into six hit points of Anchor.
design: Board topology 9 — a hazard field with one wall-lined rail through it.
design: A Stalker needs a hazard on one side of you and a tile it can stand on directly opposite. Inside the rail at x=3 both flanks are walls, so no shove exists there at all. The open east field is the fast route and the Stalkers own every tile of it. The rail's north mouth is corked by an Anchor.
retired: Half the roster (Anchor + one Stalker) takes zero actions in eight rounds; `hz-04` states the same inversion and plays.

spawn n = Anchor
spawn s = Stalker
spawn h = Husk

roster a: Wardbearer, Vanguard
roster b: Archer, Threadcaster

board:
  ...n.s.BB
  ..#.#..OB
  ..#.#.^H.
  ..#.#O..h
  ..#.#..^.
  OA#.#....
  AA...s...
